Under the OI Rules 2022, a registered trust or society that works in education or has set up hospitals in India may invest in a foreign entity with prior RBI approval, if:
• the foreign entity is in the same sector;
• the trust has existed for at least 3 financial years;
• the trust deed permits the investment;
• the trustees approve it;
• no special licence from MHA or a local authority is needed (given).
EHT runs a hospital and has been registered since 2012, so (i) ODI is permitted ✓. (ii) Approval comes from RBI, not the Central Government ✗. (iii) The deed has no clause, so it must be amended ✓. (iv) The foreign entity must be in the same sector, not just any charitable sector ✗.

